{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1337359-kindred-and-the-god-machine","id":1337359,"title":"Kindred and the God Machine","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-09-22T13:34:58-07:00","id":1337359,"title":"Kindred and the God Machine","content":"I've been spending a little time toying with the concept of the God Machine and how it would interact with Kindred existence and culture. As yet, I've only heard of a single minor covenant with any particular attachment to this... deity? Unknowable Cosmic Horror? Whatever the case may be. <br /> <br /> The Kindred, as I understand them, possess a certain earnestness of ego stemming from a need for control. This is born from the Beast and the constant, perpetual knowledge of their own fragility. Ever present is the worry that their will and being will be subsumed by the whiles of the ravenous monster that is inside them and the inevitable degradation of who they fundamentally are. As a result they cling to whatever it is that grants them a sense of stability, an immalleable &quot;truth&quot; by which they can conduct themselves in an uncertain world of darkness. This psychological need is deeply human, but the Kindred feel it in a way that far surpasses our understanding because we are neither immortal nor possessed of a semi-sapient monstrous Other. This also makes them prime candidates for stories involving mind-shattering, Lovecraftian-esque horrors that are capable of subverting their &quot;truths&quot; beyond the capacity for rationalization.<br /> <br /> As for the God Machine itself, it's a touch more complicated. The problem with unknowable cosmic powers who have active control over the fabric of reality is that they are... well... unknowable. <br /> <br /> How have you utilized the God Machine in your chronicles? What interest does your iteration of the God Machine have in Kindred, if any? Has it, in your vision of the World of Darkness, had any appreciable effect on the Kindred throughout history?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25372-ssudd387","name":"Ssudd387","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T14:27:47-07:00","id":1337372,"title":"","content":"I'm throwing this out there because it always ends up banging around in my head whenever I think of this topic: VII.<br /> <br /> I've always loved the idea of VII. Bizarre motivations, menacing iconography, blind conviction to a cause they don't seem to fully understand. Thus far, my favorite vision of VII was from the 1E Covenant Book, specifically The Sleepers. I liked the concept, but the presentation of what they were and what motivated them (not to mention how young they were in comparison to the Kindred as a whole) wasn't really for me. I'd thought of VII as something older, something that has harried the Kindred for as long as they've known, something that exists outside of any moralistic belief. I have my own issues with the Golconda angle, but that's another story. I liked the purity of the Sleeper personality, an aspect without pity or remorse, a deadly functionary in undead flesh bound to a program that it doesn't need to understand to execute on.<br /> <br /> My potential homebrew iteration ties them to the God Machine and its Angels. Their origins are ancient, but unknown. They keep no records, honor no heroes. There is no higher calling than their directive. Technically they are no longer Kindred as is properly known. The process of creating a sleeper effectively amputates the Beast, grafting in its stead a &quot;mechanical&quot; facsimile. This prosthetic mimics the Beast's behavior most of the time, enough that it's sufficiently convincing to others. For the sleeper, it feels fundamentally wrong in ways they can't quite put their finger on. This prosthetic waits, watches, measures and transmits. When it becomes active, the Kindred is technically in Frenzy with all of the accompanied dissociation. Functionally speaking, VII sleepers behave like white blood cells, dutifully culling irritants and &quot;correcting&quot; imbalances in accordance with whatever holistic sense defines their actions. I'm still working on the origins of their more ritualized behavior, their connection to certain icons and some of the underlying lore (fallen king, rising city, mark of the betrayer, etc.). The idea needs some work, certainly, and I'd welcome any suggestions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25372,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25372-ssudd387","user":"Ssudd387","date":". 09-22-2019, 05:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25372-ssudd387","name":"Ssudd387","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-23T04:34:52-07:00","id":1337467,"title":"","content":"I think tying VII to the God Machine is certainly a option. You could also use Strix as some sort of Angles or tie them in another way to the GM. Maybe the Kindreds origin lies within a failed experiment of the GM. Or they are the result of a glitch. VII and/or the Stix are the Gms answer to correct that.<br /> <br /> Oh, and there is this snipped in the brief 2e write up for the Julii:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201c<span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular, serif\">Or they raised their own Masquerade, hiding from the other Kindred, building</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular, serif\">an even greater Camarilla on the dark side of the moon, where they converse with immaculate machines.&quot;</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25507-nobby","name":"nobby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25507_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-23T08:22:55-07:00","id":1337501,"title":"","content":"Demon: The Descent Storyteller's Guide talks a bit about Kindred and Strix in relation to demons, angels and the God-Machine. It's only five pages or so, but it might be an interesting read (especially what's said about Strix) for this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-23T08:48:59-07:00","id":1337503,"title":"","content":"Hey. Thanks for the replies! <br /> <br /> The Kindred-as-failed-experiment is an interesting idea. How I've been approaching the GM's relationship to the Kindred is one of curious disdain. Whatever facet of that higher intellect that takes an interest in our tiny lives views the Kindred as an impossibility, an unnatural variable in whatever hellish algorithm defines its husbandry of the cosmos. They're parasitic perpetual motion machines, primal and (theoretically) eternal, but still so flawed and human. Naturally, that would need to be addressed. <br /> <br /> VII could easily serve in that respect. Those whose actions and projected futures who do not serve to benefit its influence are targeted while others are left alone. Then again, so could the Ordo Dracul; a sire-less Kindred, supposedly cursed by divinity, founds a Covenant based on the principle of perpetual self-modification. It's potential GM intervention, an attempt to render Kindred en masse into something more appropriate to its sense of what should and should not be. They're all options. <br /> <br /> The Strix... I feel like the Strix are something else, removed from the God Machine. A facet of whatever &quot;natural order&quot; served as Kindred origins. I personally saw the Strix as the dark truth behind the Golconda myth. The idea is just so pie-in-the-sky, it translates to me like the Disney adaptation of a Grimm fairy tale; it glosses over the blood, murder, dismemberment, and every other affront to decency in favor of a more friendly, palatable tale where everyone lives happily ever after. &quot;Of course, you'll defeat your Beast and spend eternity prancing through the woods like an undead nymph! You certainly won't fuse together with it into a horrible, owl-shaped chimera made of bestial cunning, human bitterness and smoke. Certainly not...&quot; But that's a topic for another time.<br /> <br /> Tessie: <br /> Thanks for the suggestion. It may take a tick, but I'll definitely take a look. It's been a slow slog to pick up 2E stuff, so I know I'm behind on established lore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25372-ssudd387","name":"Ssudd387","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-24T21:38:45-07:00","id":1337762,"title":"","content":"Vlad the Impaler as of the Constantinople Dark Era fought to oppose the servants of God. This is explicitly the God-Machine. The vampirism is related.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-26T07:16:53-07:00","id":1337975,"title":"","content":"Note that Theban sorcery may very well have god-machine origins. I don't have the books in front of me, but the sequence of events that led to Longinius finding the chamber and confronting &quot;angels&quot; smacks of ordering by the GM.<br /> <br /> The GM itself appears to operate within a directive to preserve the integrity of reality, including humanity's place in it. This of course carries no specific concern for individuals, but does mean that the GM--with it's vast but limited resources--cannot just excise all other supernatural influence from the planet without fundamentally wrecking reality as it is. Thus it manages, and will use kindred for that management as well as other agents.<br /> <br /> VII as sleeper executioners operating under a protocol as ancient as vampires sounds appealing. As does Theban == GM coding. And even Ordo = refinement directive. But there are many more ways in which a vampire could find themselves missing time, with something ticking dutifully in their chest. <br /> <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T10:17:39-07:00","id":1339212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ssudd387</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1337359-kindred-and-the-god-machine?p=1337503#post1337503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">VII could easily serve in that respect. Those whose actions and projected futures who do not serve to benefit its influence are targeted while others are left alone. Then again, so could the Ordo Dracul; a sire-less Kindred, supposedly cursed by divinity, founds a Covenant based on the principle of perpetual self-modification. It's potential GM intervention, an attempt to render Kindred en masse into something more appropriate to its sense of what should and should not be. They're all options.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe all of those - the interesting thing about machines is that the more complex they get, greater the chance of its parts/systems entering into all sorts of conflict without some sort of oversight around to adjust things. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-08T11:59:29-07:00","id":1340272,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of the GM being involved with VII.<br /> <br /> In a tangential direction, I used the GM to enforce the Masquerade in a LARP I ran. The idea was that the GM only notices stories and systems, so if it's not in the public eye and in the media, it falls under the GM radar.<br /> <br /> Vampires (and you could do this with werewolves or mages or whatever) who are too public with their activities start to manifest more and more banes. These are in power in direct proportion to how big the masquerade breach was. Eventually, agents of the GM would start to show up. In that game, VII was a program designed to stop offending vampires before they got the god-machine's attention.<br /> <br /> This was because the Strix created vampires in opposition to the GM's plans. In that game, they were a kind of parasite that fed off of cities, and thus indirectly fed off of the GM.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25692-joshua_lazarus","name":"Joshua_Lazarus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-08T20:15:16-07:00","id":1340352,"title":"","content":"Must admit that i have only the vaguest familiarity with the God Machine's mythology, what to say of connections to the kindred or their covenants.<br /> Machines, be they whole, faulty, buggy or broken, speak of a mathematic logic that doesn't map well to the Beast or kindred to me overall, so never really tried.<br /> <br /> That said vampires are creatures of stasis, age and history, so i could see their existences being used to offer glimpses upon the God-Machine, its cult and agents across the sands of time - Babbage's Machine, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dendera_light\" target=\"_blank\">Dendera Lights</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baghdad_Battery\" target=\"_blank\">Baghdad Batteries</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Analytical_Engine\" target=\"_blank\">Babbage Machine</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antikythera_mechanism\" target=\"_blank\">Antikythera Mechanism</a>, the works of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hero_of_Alexandria\" target=\"_blank\">Hero of Alexandria</a>.... sparks of inspiration beyond their times or artifacts of the secret Infrastructure of past eras? How might or not those things affect the kindred of times long past?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-08-2019, 11:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-09T09:05:25-07:00","id":1340421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1337359-kindred-and-the-god-machine?p=1340352#post1340352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Must admit that i have only the vaguest familiarity with the God Machine's mythology, what to say of connections to the kindred or their covenants.<br /> Machines, be they whole, faulty, buggy or broken, speak of a mathematic logic that doesn't map well to the Beast or kindred to me overall, so never really tried.<br /> <br /> That said vampires are creatures of stasis, age and history, so i could see their existences being used to offer glimpses upon the God-Machine, its cult and agents across the sands of time - Babbage's Machine, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dendera_light\" target=\"_blank\">Dendera Lights</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baghdad_Battery\" target=\"_blank\">Baghdad Batteries</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Analytical_Engine\" target=\"_blank\">Babbage Machine</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antikythera_mechanism\" target=\"_blank\">Antikythera Mechanism</a>, the works of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hero_of_Alexandria\" target=\"_blank\">Hero of Alexandria</a>.... sparks of inspiration beyond their times or artifacts of the secret Infrastructure of past eras? How might or not those things affect the kindred of times long past?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The GM is, by design, intended to cut across products and touch--albeit sometimes lightly--the goings-on of the supernatural in CofD. Here's my meta-understanding of it, drawn from various sources:<br /> <br /> The GM was created to stabilize reality such that parallel dimensions did not intrude, destabilize and ultimately destroy the integrity of the one both the GM and Mankind exists in (Prime). That reality, however, grinds against a variety of spiritual and mystical realms that can loosely be considered both part of and separate from Prime. Imagine a series of Venn circles, overlapping, of which one the GM is intent on keeping in good order--it thus touches all the intruding realms and has an interest, to such an extent that they impinge on Prime.<br /> <br /> Realms that are NOT naturally connected with Prime include diverse timelines, places with very different physical and spiritual rules and regions utterly corrupted by paragon concepts (thought left hanging on purpose).<br /> <br /> Examples could be: the Prince of a Thousand Leaves, alternate timelines and the like. The GM has its own mystic substrate realm it can set up and configure for its purposes, though the rules for its use and access are almost completely unknown. Somehow mechanisms are required for its use, which implies rules that may be exceedingly complex but probably not shifting. The mystical realms that impinge on Prime, however, DO shift, and over time the GM itself has broken and very imperfectly performs its created job.<br /> <br /> You could imagine a perfect, ticking world in which Mankind goes on about its business without the supernatural touching anything, anywhere--that *might* be what the GM desires. What it gets is a pragmatically managed reality in which it has to constantly fight fires that threaten to consume both it and Mankind in soul-shattering chaos. There are probably constant forks going on, and GM devices emplaced to KEEP such forks apart, lest natural sympathy crash dimensions together....<br /> <br /> Whew, ok.<br /> <br /> So vampires are a supernatural element; a parasitical intrusion on Prime that began at some point probably due to corruption from another, spiritual realm. Despite any early efforts, they have persisted but are not, in general, hostile to Mankind or the integrity of reality. They break some ideal rules, notably persisting much longer than the minds of Man do, and as such may accumulate glitches that represent vectors for hostile dimensional intrusion or threats to the secrecy directive the GM follows (and that vampires generally agree with). <br /> <br /> They, like Man, occasionally require &quot;pruning&quot;. They, like Man, occasionally are useful in their unmodified state. They, like Man, occasionally are MORE useful, modified.<br /> <br /> The GM has protocols for each condition.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-15T06:12:19-07:00","id":1341429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1337359-kindred-and-the-god-machine?p=1340421#post1340421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could imagine a perfect, ticking world in which Mankind goes on about its business without the supernatural touching anything, anywhere--that *might* be what the GM desires. What it gets is a pragmatically managed reality in which it has to constantly fight fires that threaten to consume both it and Mankind in soul-shattering chaos. There are probably constant forks going on, and GM devices emplaced to KEEP such forks apart, lest natural sympathy crash dimensions together....</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess it depends on how the GM defines integrity, if isolation is the desired ideal or a certain degree of interaction with other realms is acceptable, even required, to the maitenance of the realm's integrity. Its criteria, whatever they are, would be key to its projects and determining required infrastructure to advance them.<br /> <br /> Thinking of interface between spirit realms and integrity makes me remember the plot of Hunter: the Reckoning and how a conflict in the Underworld would result in the 6th Maelstrom and a wave of ghosts being stranded on the physical world as Risen undead. And how the spontaneous rising of undead, vampires or others, might or not be seen as a less extreme/epidemic case of the same phenomenon.<br /> <br /> Some bug - or feature, depends on how problematic or necessary one considers it - of the life, death and/or reincarnation/ressurection cycle. But a limited one and acceptable. Who knows, the existence of undead might be a sort of pylon, the hinges that keep the gates between the realms of living and dead from corroding and breaking down or sealing shut. Strange but a stable component of the system.<br /> <br /> At least until a draugr/larvae/revenant wave sets in, that is. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Could the GM be the force behind <b><i>Humanity</i></b>, contributing to the kindred <i>remembering </i>being human and acting upon it, to serve as defense mechanism of sorts against their own and consequently preserving stability to a certain degree? The rational, organized kindred <i><b>are </b></i>a major factor in the elimination and restraining of the more bestial - and epidemic-prone - of their kind. Hmm, food for thought...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-15-2019, 09:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-15T09:12:17-07:00","id":1341453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1337359-kindred-and-the-god-machine?p=1341429#post1341429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess it depends on how the GM defines integrity, if isolation is the desired ideal or a certain degree of interaction with other realms is acceptable, even required, to the maitenance of the realm's integrity. Its criteria, whatever they are, would be key to its projects and determining required infrastructure to advance them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any consideration of the GM should best be done in terms of machines and code. There are programming languages--and physical devices--that force a designer or operator to do things in a certain way even if that defies unenlightened observation. Take the human eye: it flips images upside down as they are delivered to the brain for post-processing reversion. What a F-ed-up design! How did this happen? Yet it seems to be the most efficient solution to a set of complex problems, and as such the additional mental effort required for vision is... accommodated.<br /> <br /> Similarly, if you wall-off the Hisil from reality you get... spiritually dead areas and people. So they have to be permitted to co-exist in some proximity lest humanity lose something important, and that proximity means the risk of <i>constant</i> incursion by predatory alien creatures kept in check only by other, multi-dimensional organisms. It's a freaking mess, but not one the GM has been able, to date, to engineer around. It may not be <i>capable</i> of engineering around it--even if its directives told it too.<br /> <br /> But that won't keep it from trying. Some.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thinking of interface between spirit realms and integrity makes me remember the plot of Hunter: the Reckoning and how a conflict in the Underworld would result in the 6th Maelstrom and a wave of ghosts being stranded on the physical world as Risen undead. And how the spontaneous rising of undead, vampires or others, might or not be seen as a less extreme/epidemic case of the same phenomenon.<br /> <br /> Some bug - or feature, depends on how problematic or necessary one considers it - of the life, death and/or reincarnation/ressurection cycle. But a limited one and acceptable. Who knows, the existence of undead might be a sort of pylon, the hinges that keep the gates between the realms of living and dead from corroding and breaking down or sealing shut. Strange but a stable component of the system. </div> </div> </div>Exactly: least-worst solution to deviation from optimal design principles.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At least until a draugr/larvae/revenant wave sets in, that is. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Could the GM be the force behind <b><i>Humanity</i></b>, contributing to the kindred <i>remembering </i>being human and acting upon it, to serve as defense mechanism of sorts against their own and consequently preserving stability to a certain degree? The rational, organized kindred <i><b>are </b></i>a major factor in the elimination and restraining of the more bestial - and epidemic-prone - of their kind. Hmm, food for thought... </div> </div> </div>Possible. Consider Humanity as a kind of reactor control rod to what would otherwise be the immediate inversion of the human condition into its most bestial, predatory and uncontrolled state. In other words, the full Claim-ing of a mortal body by a Hisil-like spirit-entity's behavior patterns (if not, in fact, a spirit-entity).<br /> <br /> If the Vitae-borne Curse is a sort of spiritual virus, and viruses run on genetic code, then the GM may have acted to corrupt that code early on and provide for Humanity's persistence as a stabilizing element.<br /> <br /> Why it would do so, however, is probably best imagined through the lens of a future in which the world really is consumed by draugr plagues--which the GM acted in the past in order to prevent.<br /> <br /> No wonder the Strix are so pissed.<br /> <br /> One wonders which infrastructure maintains the integrity of Humanity extant across vampire-kinds(s)?<br /> <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-15T18:36:03-07:00","id":1341543,"title":"","content":"Hmm, must admit i'm liking the direction this seems to be taking, the idea of a cosmic/enviromental role of sorts of undead, as a kind of valve of sorts that maintains a basic degree of exchange between the realms of living and dead by their mere existence and this phenomenon might be necessary to humanity's continued survival - what incidentally could imply two apocalyptic scenarios the GM rebooted the Prime from:<br /> <br /> - the world that is consumed by draugr plagues.<br /> - the world where the complete extermination of vampires leads to eventual erosion of connections between Prime and Underworld, messing with life-death-renewal cycle, or to an active pursuit of its maintenance by humanity, an awareness that eventually leads in the blossoming of necromantic empires and gross misuse of such lore and power of the flow ripping the gates between life and death assunder, with even more apocalyptic results (could Mummy: the Curse relate to this somehow?).<br /> <br /> About infrastructure maintains the integrity of Humanity extant across vampire-kinds(s), i just remembered a story hook from the Immortals &quot;blue book&quot;...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Immortals, pg.29</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 <b>Common Blood</b>: The Bathing Ritual and vampirism share an ancestry. Vampires, for many years, were mindless predators. The Embrace granted immortality, but it also removed the higher brain functions. Then, a Babylonian king called En Isiratuu was made a vampire. His advisors and high priests, not wishing to see their beloved master fall to bloodthirsty madness, developed the Bathing Ritual to give him not physical immortality (which he already had), but spiritual and mental immortality. The Ritual then spread, and was used on other vampires, granting them sentience until the old bestial undead were all but eradicated. Now, thousands of years later, descendants of this vampire-king have learned what the Bathing Ritual has become, and are dedicated to wiping it out \u2014 but doing so might damn vampires to insanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a hook it's more a concept for a ST to pick or not than fluff, but felt most relevant to tie into the subject, specially considering his connection to the origins of the Iltani and En bloodlines, the &quot;Black Streets of Babylon&quot; era/settting and maybe the Akhud or Belial's Brood* (if not both).<br /> <br /> *According to a number of their sources/factions, the covenant/cult would have a start in Babylon, with a vampire whose name is recorded variously as <i><b>En</b></i>kara, <i><b>En</b></i>hidir and <i><b>En</b></i>khatur.<br /> <br /> As an aside, the other two Requiem-related hooks, about the potential of a blood bather's victims rising up as near-mindless, weaker, pack-oriented vampires or a group of Belial's Brood coming across a blood bather and starting to worship it, could also fit into such a infrastructure-building process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-15-2019, 09:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T09:13:47-07:00","id":1341637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1337359-kindred-and-the-god-machine?p=1341543#post1341543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, must admit i'm liking the direction this seems to be taking, the idea of a cosmic/enviromental role of sorts of undead, as a kind of valve of sorts that maintains a basic degree of exchange between the realms of living and dead by their mere existence and this phenomenon might be necessary to humanity's continued survival - what incidentally could imply two apocalyptic scenarios the GM rebooted the Prime from:<br /> <br /> - the world that is consumed by draugr plagues.<br /> - the world where the complete extermination of vampires leads to eventual erosion of connections between Prime and Underworld, messing with life-death-renewal cycle, or to an active pursuit of its maintenance by humanity, an awareness that eventually leads in the blossoming of necromantic empires and gross misuse of such lore and power of the flow ripping the gates between life and death assunder, with even more apocalyptic results (could Mummy: the Curse relate to this somehow?).</div> </div> </div> </div>While a given campaign will vary considerably, the broader discussion should acknowledge that as creatures with underworld connections go, vampires are pretty far down the list. Geist and Mummy are there first (as are Mages, we won't talk about them). <br /> <br /> I'm happy to imagine vampires are GM-related control rods, however please note that they are first and foremost thematically the extension of human urges to extreme degrees, unbounded by mortality or mores. <b><i>That's</i></b> the challenge they present, and the idea of the vampire is that the challenge is both seductive and utterly destructive to the character of people even exposed to it. (&quot;The truth shall set you free...&quot; to fall into a destruction of temptation or corrosive worry and paranoia, until you respond to others with all the rage and fear of the Beast you run from.)<br /> <br /> Wandering aside for the moment:<br /> <br /> Vampire persistence offers the GM something useful that it could employ as an anchor for its infrastructure. These are extremely stable physical entities which, when properly prepared, could host infrastructure touchpoints and extensively folded machinery for doing... um... whatever needs to be done, really. In a mobile package with only somewhat greater risks over static emplacements. And much less risk over humans, which are quite fragile, really.<br /> <br /> I'm likely to use this approach for a PC who has, for reasons, been rendered &quot;protected&quot; from time wonky-hoey business. The GM will use him to ensure aberrant timelines and entities gain minimal purchase. The risks of doing so are only moderate and within acceptable parameters, while much less expensive than maintaining another angel or several. It's unlikely that someone will cut him open to discover intricate Antikythera mechanisms etched with iridium into his breastbone, and it is unlikely the infrastructure will be subjected to spiritual pressure sufficient to deform it.<br /> <br /> Unlikely.<br /> <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T13:52:37-07:00","id":1341704,"title":"","content":"Well, if memory serves from the Demon line, Strix are known to nest and corrupt G-M infrastructure, and Angels have a kill on sight program when it comes to the Strix.<br /> <br /> Now, looking between the Strix and Kindred relations, we know that Strix on some inherent level don't like kindred for a myriad of reasons, and according to Demon the Strix can provide some strange insights on the God Machine, despite claiming to have no memory or reason as to why they would know these things.<br /> <br /> Now, as we all know, Infrastructure is meant to do whatever the G-M needs to keep the status quo. Strix originally might stem from some dark shadowy place from before time, but most form here and now. One thing all Strix ro agree on is that their is some inherent connection between Kindred and Strix.<br /> <br /> So, maybe looking at the Kindred as some great cosmic tool might not be the only approach. An originally antagonistic force on reality might be a fun approach to consider.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T07:48:08-07:00","id":1341858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1337359-kindred-and-the-god-machine?p=1341704#post1341704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, if memory serves from the Demon line, Strix are known to nest and corrupt G-M infrastructure, and Angels have a kill on sight program when it comes to the Strix.<br /> <br /> Now, looking between the Strix and Kindred relations, we know that Strix on some inherent level don't like kindred for a myriad of reasons, and according to Demon the Strix can provide some strange insights on the God Machine, despite claiming to have no memory or reason as to why they would know these things.<br /> <br /> Now, as we all know, Infrastructure is meant to do whatever the G-M needs to keep the status quo. Strix originally might stem from some dark shadowy place from before time, but most form here and now. One thing all Strix ro agree on is that their is some inherent connection between Kindred and Strix.<br /> <br /> So, maybe looking at the Kindred as some great cosmic tool might not be the only approach. An originally antagonistic force on reality might be a fun approach to consider.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What if... things are backward: the vampiric curse virus was originally a kind of GM infrastructure that was subsequently corrupted by the Strix. Only they were unable to fully accomplish what they intended to do, and so despise vampires who cling to some form of &quot;original programming&quot;.<br /> <br /> You could tie this to accounts of early humans living for enormous spans of time (ok, centuries)--they benefited from GM stabilizing protocols that were subsequently corrupted. The GM cannot simply go in and rip out the core human infrastructure that underpins this, as it would destroy humanity. Perhaps relate this to theories of mitochondria as cellular elements descended from specialized bacteria? (Yes, Virginia, the human organism is already a hybrid creature, and you personal DNA changes frequently!)<br /> <br /> If you stop and think, immortal humans would contribute to the objective of reality stasis with humanity at its center. It's more manageable than a constant churn of ensouled individuals who are aging, dying and being replaced--a logistically messy situation with significant and uncapture-able risks.<br /> <br /> So what might be the original objectives of the Strix in this? If the theory is correct that vampires can evolve into Strix-form, then they are interested in propagation. They hate humanity because humans are both food and unrealized Strix kept from becoming &quot;them&quot; because of the GM (among other things).<br /> <br /> The link between Strix and GM could explain their early origins, in the sense that the GM itself plays fast-and-loose with chronological ordering. So the Strix may have inserted themselves into prehistory using similar protocols in their attempt to affect the original corruption of human cellular infrastructure. You could even run a campaign in which one or several Strix are attempting to gain access to infrastructure that will enable them to fold time and accomplish this. You could even explain the scatter-minded nature of individual Strix through their appearance recursively through time as they fought/fight a battle with the GM to locate and rewrite the nature of humanity.<br /> <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12493,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","user":"Khanwulf","date":". 10-17-2019, 10:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-20T12:11:14-07:00","id":1342561,"title":"","content":"In mereology (the philisophical study of how parts create wholes), there is one theory called Universalism, which states that any two objects compose a third. <br /> <br /> In the philosophy of mind, there is a problem with functionalism. Functionalism is the theory that mental states are defined by their causal roles - both in how you enter that state, and which behaviors and mental states it might lead to. The problem is that any thing with complex enough states that are causully related would be judged by functionalism to have a mind. An economy might have a mind.<br /> <br /> Put the two together. My theory is that the GM came up with civilization. Civilization literally is infrastructure. Maybe the GM existed elsewhere before civilization, it would be composed of slow, ultimately basic components. But the development of civilization would be a massive upgrade. Without civilization, the GM would effectively become braindead. In some sense, civilization *is* the GM. <br /> <br /> In parallell, all vampires are a kind of social parasite. They require large populations to sustain themselves, laws and customs to exploit and subvert for protection. <br /> <br /> In the civilization-as-GM-brain theory, vampires are quite literally a disease. A cancer or virus. The interaction of strix and infrastructure may be the most exotic examples of an interaction that is already writ-small in the kindred and human society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24634,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","user":"DubiousRuffian","date":".  Spelling 10-20-2019, 08:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","name":"DubiousRuffian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-20T14:04:49-07:00","id":1342577,"title":"","content":"The Holy Engineers should be of interest to this thread. Written up in the 1e book <i>Danse Macabre</i> and referenced in 2e's mention of the Julii, they are a covenant of vampires who claim to use the God-Machine as a medium to commune with their master, Death. This communication takes the form of the Radio Sickness, electromagnetic prophesies that answer questions the god talkers have yet to ask, or else destroy them, if they fail to provide the question to the answer and close the time loop.<br /> <br /> Their lore relies a lot on the writeup of the God-Machine from the 1e corebook, and so precedes ideas like Infrastructure and the Unchained, but it presents a unique relationship between vampire and immaculate Machine \u2013 not as slave and master or as enemies, but as user and tool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":97,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","user":"The MG","date":". 10-20-2019, 05:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T12:15:03-07:00","id":1342774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DubiousRuffian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1337359-kindred-and-the-god-machine?p=1342561#post1342561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In mereology (the philisophical study of how parts create wholes), there is one theory called Universalism, which states that any two objects compose a third.<br /> <br /> In the philosophy of mind, there is a problem with functionalism. Functionalism is the theory that mental states are defined by their causal roles - both in how you enter that state, and which behaviors and mental states it might lead to. The problem is that any thing with complex enough states that are causully related would be judged by functionalism to have a mind. An economy might have a mind.<br /> <br /> Put the two together. My theory is that the GM came up with civilization. Civilization literally is infrastructure. Maybe the GM existed elsewhere before civilization, it would be composed of slow, ultimately basic components. But the development of civilization would be a massive upgrade. Without civilization, the GM would effectively become braindead. In some sense, civilization *is* the GM.<br /> <br /> In parallell, all vampires are a kind of social parasite. They require large populations to sustain themselves, laws and customs to exploit and subvert for protection.<br /> <br /> In the civilization-as-GM-brain theory, vampires are quite literally a disease. A cancer or virus. The interaction of strix and infrastructure may be the most exotic examples of an interaction that is already writ-small in the kindred and human society.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bravo! But: parasites can also adapt and fall into the niche of symbiote. They join the mechanism of civilization and become part of it. The GM accepts them as normal, up until the vampire deviates from behavioral norms and triggers self-defense protocols within the body public. <br /> <br /> At that point VII gets activated, perhaps.<br /> <br /> To the extent that vampires cling to humanity, and humanity is defined as a social creature that builds systems of interaction, they will look like something that belongs. They may get caught up in the gears, so to speak, but they'll belong.<br /> <br /> Strix, on the other hand, do not. They don't seem to appreciate civilization much, and think of vampires are organisms that failed to properly coopt the host and are thus disappointments to be evolved further or destroyed. This, similarly, can help explain their (mutual) antagonism to the GM.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br /> <br /> PS. We're mapping sides of the same polyhedron when it comes to GM, Strix and vampires. They are clearly intimately related and a storyteller can pick whatever they want for an exploration into why the vamps haven't eaten a half-dozen hunter-killer angels per year.<br /> <br /> Or, maybe they have? Looking at you, Montreal!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T13:05:01-07:00","id":1342786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1337359-kindred-and-the-god-machine?p=1342774#post1342774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Bravo! But: parasites can also adapt and fall into the niche of symbiote. They join the mechanism of civilization and become part of it. The GM accepts them as normal, up until the vampire deviates from behavioral norms and triggers self-defense protocols within the body public<br /> ...<br /> Strix, on the other hand, do not. They don't seem to appreciate civilization much, and think of vampires are organisms that failed to properly coopt the host and are thus disappointments to be evolved further or destroyed. This, similarly, can help explain their (mutual) antagonism to the GM.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right, and I think that would work well in a chronicle. But I personally like to play the Kindred as absolute deviations from the natural order. That they are something that has gone horribly, horribly wrong, and are, in a very real sense abominations. Or at least that the state of vampirism is, if not the people themselves. If anything, I would think that vampirism is a <i>glitch</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1337359-kindred-and-the-god-machine?p=1342774#post1342774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or, maybe they have? Looking at you, Montreal!</div> </div> </div> </div>Ohhhhhh sheeeeeeiiiiiiittttttt<br /> <br /> Edit: Oooh, maybe VII is what happens when vampires get hooked up to the GM. Kind of like wrewriting an angel/demon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24634,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","user":"DubiousRuffian","date":". 10-21-2019, 04:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","name":"DubiousRuffian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T13:16:10-07:00","id":1342792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DubiousRuffian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1337359-kindred-and-the-god-machine?p=1342786#post1342786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're right, and I think that would work well in a chronicle. But I personally like to play the Kindred as absolute deviations from the natural order. That they are something that has gone horribly, horribly wrong, and are, in a very real sense abominations. Or at least that the state of vampirism is, if not the people themselves. If anything, I would think that vampirism is a <i>glitch</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Ohhhhhh sheeeeeeiiiiiiittttttt<br /> <br /> Edit: Oooh, maybe VII is what happens when vampires get hooked up to the GM. Kind of like wrewriting an angel/demon.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Working backwards: that's been a decent theory--that VII are vamps integrated into infrastructure and harnessed as antibodies by the GM. Perhaps... &quot;prions&quot; is a better analogy, since HK angels and the like would be the white-blood cell obliterators of the body politic.<br /> <br /> Anyway: yes I agree, vamps should be utter deviations. They are the tapeworms that you ignore because it doesn't eat much and taking the meds leaves you sicker for a time. Scale up to worldwide systems (may of which are broken anyway), and you can tolerate a lot of deviation before applying meds selectively in a game of abomination wack-a-mole. <br /> <br /> Vampirism needs to ruin everything. It's part of the equation. Whether vampirism is a glitch in human bio-infrastructure or a convergent curse or an alien infestation it <i>shouldn't</i> be there and bears no constructive fruit in an absolute sense. It <i>may</i> be <i>made</i> useful. Sometimes. <br /> <br /> But ripping out the infestation is akin to the parable of the planter and the tares (weeds), who planted a field of good wheat, an enemy came and sowed with tares, and when alerted of the contamination the owner demurred to rip them out until harvest--when the plants would be easily distinguishable from each other. Until that point it would be too easy to tear big chunks of productive field up just to get the annoying weeds.<br /> <br /> Ditto vamps. Ticks dug in.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T13:37:15-07:00","id":1342797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1337359-kindred-and-the-god-machine?p=1342792#post1342792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Working backwords... Ditto vamps. Ticks dug in.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>I very much dig all of that.<br /> <br /> Slightly unrelated, but I think you could get a really cool chronicle of Demon where you're on the run from some covenant that's gotten a taste for Angel/Demon blood. I'm not too sure how to differentiate it from a standard Demon game, but I think there are some interesting possibilities. Maybe they'd work better as secondary antagonists. <br /> <br /> Like, you're doing your standard &quot;fight the angels&quot; thing, and you need the help of the local vampire domain, but also need to hide your nature from them, or else they'll try to diablerize you. Maybe you've been outed to one dude, but you're a respected not-member of the court. And as long as you're in public, you're safe. But he's really trying to get you alone in an alleyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","name":"DubiousRuffian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T05:27:38-07:00","id":1343969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DubiousRuffian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1337359-kindred-and-the-god-machine?p=1342797#post1342797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I very much dig all of that.<br /> <br /> Slightly unrelated, but I think you could get a really cool chronicle of Demon where you're on the run from some covenant that's gotten a taste for Angel/Demon blood. I'm not too sure how to differentiate it from a standard Demon game, but I think there are some interesting possibilities. Maybe they'd work better as secondary antagonists.<br /> <br /> Like, you're doing your standard &quot;fight the angels&quot; thing, and you need the help of the local vampire domain, but also need to hide your nature from them, or else they'll try to diablerize you. Maybe you've been outed to one dude, but you're a respected not-member of the court. And as long as you're in public, you're safe. But he's really trying to get you alone in an alleyway.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, this set-up on itself brings some questions to mind, stuff onne would have to adress beforehand:<br /> <br /> - vampires are not exactly familiar with GM's angels &amp; demons and i have no idea of how familiar those angels &amp; demons are with the most active types of supernatural beings.<br /> <br /> - Looking for the blood of other supernaturals requires predating or at least interacting with those other supernaturals, so inherently risky and not something most kindred will risk themselves for out of curiosity. Getting <i>actual benefits</i> from drinking such blood usually require certain merits and making something of a regular practice out of this drinking and consequently an experienced and powerful vampire.<br /> <br /> - Diablerie is even more complicated, as it goes much beyond blood, into consumption of the soul (or somethnig akin to it) and can be done only to other vampires, except fot those few that learned the Coil of the Locust (apocryphal coil, from the Ordo Draacul book) or strange powers to make such a thing possible.<br /> <br /> So, possible it might be, for this kind of scenario to come up this way requires coming up with some questions, answers and niches/backstory bits to fit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-27-2019, 08:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T14:52:57-07:00","id":1344074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1337359-kindred-and-the-god-machine?p=1343969#post1343969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, this set-up on itself brings some questions to mind, stuff onne would have to adress beforehand:<br /> <br /> - vampires are not exactly familiar with GM's angels &amp; demons and i have no idea of how familiar those angels &amp; demons are with the most active types of supernatural beings.<br /> <br /> - Looking for the blood of other supernaturals requires predating or at least interacting with those other supernaturals, so inherently risky and not something most kindred will risk themselves for out of curiosity. Getting <i>actual benefits</i> from drinking such blood usually require certain merits and making something of a regular practice out of this drinking and consequently an experienced and powerful vampire.<br /> <br /> - Diablerie is even more complicated, as it goes much beyond blood, into consumption of the soul (or somethnig akin to it) and can be done only to other vampires, except fot those few that learned the Coil of the Locust (apocryphal coil, from the Ordo Draacul book) or strange powers to make such a thing possible.<br /> <br /> So, possible it might be, for this kind of scenario to come up this way requires coming up with some questions, answers and niches/backstory bits to fit.</div> </div> </div> </div>An angel did it. Probably to create a self sustaining Demon detection system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T18:27:06-07:00","id":1344104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1337359-kindred-and-the-god-machine?p=1344074#post1344074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> An angel did it. Probably to create a self sustaining Demon detection system.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, because &quot;An angel did it&quot; is such a great set-up to add a new layer/threat to a Demon game.... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Not to mention - aren't demons rogue angels, meaning that vampires after demon blood might also hunt angels too, because they don't know - or care - for the difference, making them an awful demon detection system? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Not that i know much about Demon: Descent, just a thought or two while we are at it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T21:25:57-07:00","id":1344121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1337359-kindred-and-the-god-machine?p=1344104#post1344104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, because &quot;An angel did it&quot; is such a great set-up to add a new layer/threat to a Demon game.... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Angels are agents of the God-Machine, built to purpose often for the specific end of accomplishing a goal beyond the reach of cultists and other dupes. The form they take that gives demons the most trouble happens to do so because the God-Machine lets them sidestep the entire system of Manifestation to wear false flesh and walk among the mortal herd.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not to mention - aren't demons rogue angels, meaning that vampires after demon blood might also hunt angels too, because they don't know - or care - for the difference, making them an awful demon detection system? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>Demons are rogue angels and therefore are cut off from all the things angels commonly benefit from through their connection to the God-Machine, chief among them being access to their own layer of Twilight and provision of maintenance that prevents their long-term cover identities from degrading in convincingness to the point where their forename falls off and their wardrobe is literally identical copies of the same outfit.<br /> <br /> Demons are much easier to find on purpose than angels \u2014 the Unchained can fall victim to individual slip-ups, but angels reveal themselves on purpose from a position of power when ordered to, and it's only the fact that the thing giving them their orders is big, busy, and fallible that makes these occasions not advance Step Forty-Seven of an intricate and ever-unfolding Plan to the appropriate drop point.<br /> <br /> An angel only needs to engineer stigmata in a population of vampires to make them dramatically better-equipped to locate any major work of the God-Machine that isn't deliberately hidden, and in an area where such a confidence scheme is in place, the God-Machine <i>absolutely</i> throws a sheet over everything it hasn't already slated for demolition in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}